{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And Moses charged, with the elders of Israel\"</b> is that after Moses finished his words, he charged the elders that they too should speak along with him and admonish the people to keep all the commandments, for every people follows the counsel of its elders. And it is written: <b>\"which I command you\"</b>, and not <b>\"which we command\"</b>, because the principal discourse is Moses', and the elders lift up their voice saying to the people: hear, listen, and do. So too: <b>\"And Moses and the priests the Levites spoke to all Israel\"</b> (Deuteronomy 27:9) — for the priests said to the people: <b>\"Attend and hear, O Israel\"</b>, while Moses said: <b>\"This day you have become a people\"</b>. But Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 27:1) that <b>\"keep all the commandment\"</b> refers to the commandment of the stones, which he will mention. This is not correct."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:05.006895057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}